<ResourceDictionary
    xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml">

    <!--
        Transcribed 1:1 from the `d` values of the `I` map in mini-ios2.jsx and
        the `P` map in mini-ios2-more.jsx. SVG path syntax and XAML abbreviated
        geometry syntax share the same command letters, so these port verbatim
        apart from re-tokenising every number with an explicit space separator
        (WinUI's parser will not split "6-6" or "0h16" the way an SVG one does).

        Source viewBox is 0 0 24 24 for all of them. StrokeIcon renders them on a
        24x24 Canvas inside a Viewbox, which reproduces SVG viewBox semantics
        exactly — including stroke width scaling with the icon.
    -->

    <!--
        PathGeometry rather than Geometry: Geometry is abstract, and WinUI's
        parser cannot make one out of a string the way WPF's type converter
        does. Declared as <Geometry> these compiled without complaint and then
        failed at runtime with "Failed to assign to property StrokeIcon.Data",
        which took down every window that shows an icon, i.e. all of them.
        Figures takes the same abbreviated path syntax the SVG came in.
    -->

